Want a tiny SwiftUI List reference to avoid typos? Examples:
- Basic List:
  struct ContentView: View {
    var body: some View {
      List {
        Text("Row 1")
        Text("Row 2")
      }
    }
  }
- With data:
  struct ContentView: View {
    let items = ["A", "B", "C"]
    var body: some View {
      List(items, id: \.self) { item in
        Text(item)
      }
    }
  }
Common gotchas: capital L in List; body returns some View so you can omit 'return'; ForEach needs an id. Want me to adapt this to your data?

